## Jetson Development

| Machine | Workspace | Access |
|---------|-----------|--------|
| Dev PC | `~/maher_ws` | local |
| Jetson | `~/maher_ws` | `ssh ubuntu@192.168.2.138` (DHCP — update if changed; alias `jetrover` may work) |

**Bringup (Jetson):** `start_app_node.service` is **enabled and starts automatically** on every Jetson boot — it brings up camera, lidar, IMU, ekf, servo, odom, rosbridge, web_video_server. **Leave it running.** Only `sudo systemctl stop start_app_node.service` if a project node conflicts with vendor nodes. Verify it's up with `systemctl is-active start_app_node.service`.

**Workspace overlay pattern (Jetson):** Two workspaces, source underlay first then overlay:

```bash
ssh jetrover
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash                          # ROS distro
source /home/ubuntu/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash              # underlay (vendor bringup)
source /home/ubuntu/maher_ws/install/setup.bash             # overlay (your projects)
```

- Underlay: `/home/ubuntu/ros2_ws` — vendor stack (`bringup`, `simulations/jetrover_description`, `driver/*`, `interfaces`, etc.). Service runs nodes from here. Read-only — see `vendor/README.md`.
- Overlay: `/home/ubuntu/maher_ws` — your projects (`src/Recognition-of-Different-Colored-Cubes`, `src/jetrover_description`, `src/2D-LiDAR-Mapping-with-SLAM`). Renamed from `jetson_ws` on 2026-07-08.
- Helper workspace: `/home/ubuntu/third_party_ros2/third_party_ws` — vendor helpers (IMU calib, lidar filters, AprilTag, RF2O). Auto-loaded by vendor bringup via `/home/ubuntu/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash`.

**Build this package on Jetson (after editing):**

```bash
ssh jetrover
cd /home/ubuntu/maher_ws
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
source install/setup.bash
colcon build --packages-select recognition_of_different_colored_cubes --symlink-install
```

**DDS: Fast DDS (`rmw_fastrtps_cpp`), not Cyclone.** The `fastdds.xml` on both machines configures unicast `initialPeersList` to the other machine's IP. Dev PC: `/home/maher/fastdds.xml` (peers → 192.168.2.138). Jetson: `/home/ubuntu/fastdds.xml` (peers → 192.168.2.102). Do **not** set `RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_cyclonedds_cpp` — it won't find the Jetson's discovery endpoints.

