## Current Status

**Active milestone:** **M5 PARTIAL** (implementation complete, acceptance gate failing). The M5 PARTIAL verdict from M5c2 (2026-06-28) is a confirmed model-accuracy issue, not a lighting/optics issue — see canonical 2026-06-28 M5c2 entry in [`docs/LOGBOOK.md`](docs/LOGBOOK.md) and [`evaluation/m5_live/report.md`](evaluation/m5_live/report.md) for the live-evidence summary.

**Active step:** Decide how to fix the positive-detection gap. Three paths on the table (see `evaluation/m5_live/report.md` §11.7 and `docs/m3d-revived-plan.md` for full detail):

1. **Fine-tune on JetRover-room images** — `docs/m3d-revived-plan.md` (955 lines, 2026-06-28) specifies 80 new RGB frames + Roboflow positives, 30 epochs at lr0=0.0005 from `models/best.pt`, then re-export → ONNX → TensorRT. ~3-4 calendar days, one Maher physical capture session at the Jetson. Recommended path.
2. **Lower confidence threshold** — already tried in M5c2; only unlocks green_cube (2/439), red and blue stay at zero. Insufficient on its own.
3. **Document M5 PARTIAL** — accepts the project does not meet its primary success criteria (≥80% accuracy, ≥5 fps). Rejected for portfolio reasons.

The 5 open questions in `docs/m3d-revived-plan.md` §9 (capture spec, Roboflow project choice, val split, calendar budget, fallback policy) are Maher's decisions; the M3d plan recommends defaults for all 5. Decisions will be recorded in `docs/m3d-decided.md` when made (NOT in kanban comments — see Working mode below).

**Last completed step:** M5c2 sticker-removed re-test (2026-06-28). Same scene as M5c but with the dimming sticker removed from the Orbbec RGB camera: KEEP=0/460 at conf=0.50 (no change vs M5c 0/414) and KEEP=2/439 at conf=0.25 (only green_cube detected; red and blue still zero). This confirms the M5 PARTIAL verdict is a model issue, not a sticker issue.

**Working mode (changed 2026-06-28):** Kanban workflow is **OFF**. The robotics-tutor profile is now the only agent (no implementer / researcher / tester / documenter / architect / orchestrator profiles in active use). Maher decides the role at each turn ("plan this", "research this", "implement this", "document this", "review this"). Decisions between sessions live in project files, not kanban comments. The kanban DB at `~/.hermes/kanban/boards/colored-cube-recognition/kanban.db` is read-only history. See `docs/learn/NOTES.md` "Working mode" section for full implications.

**Prior steps (kept for history):**

M4c1 supersedes the prior "raise conf to 0.50 or fine-tune on JetRover-room images" recommendation from the M4b card; the geometry filter is the **necessary** part of the M5 pre-ship gate, the fine-tune is the **conditional** part if Phase 1 leaves residual FPs on V3 or on a tight-bbox real cube.

M5c2 (2026-06-28, kanban card `t_737dbf1a`): sticker-removed re-test, confirmed model-accuracy issue, not sticker/lighting issue. 0/460 KEEP at conf=0.50; 2/439 KEEP at conf=0.25 (green only). See `evaluation/m5_live/report.md` §12 for the full bag analysis.

M5 implementation COMPLETE: cube_detection_node (29 rclpy parameters, 3 publishers, latency logging), geometry filter as a proper package module, TensorRT FP16 backend, RGB+depth sync, camera intrinsics loading. Models at the time of M5c2: `models/best.engine` SHA-256 `c64d3e5e…` (matches M4a — no retraining), `models/best_hardneg.pt` (18.5 MB, M3c hard-negative fine-tune, frozen at 2026-06-27).

M4c1 supersedes; M3c (hard-negative fine-tune with `best_hardneg.pt`) closed 2026-06-27 as no-longer-needed for the V3 scope but kept as fallback. The M3d-revived plan (`docs/m3d-revived-plan.md`) flips the scope from hard-negative rejection (already solved by geometry filter) to positive detection on real JetRover-room cubes.

M4/M6 evaluation data — Phase A complete: 30 empty-scene JetRover RGB frames (640×360, q=92) captured from `/depth_cam/rgb/image_raw` on 2026-06-27 into `evaluation/camera_samples/empty_2026-06-27/` (gitignored), with `empty_metadata.json` sidecar (30/30 SHA-256 verified). Capture harness is `scripts/capture_frames.py` (Jetson-side rclpy subscriber saver) + `scripts/verify_camera_samples.py` (dev-PC-side sidecar checker). Phase B (cube-arranged captures at 20/40/60/80 cm per `docs/evaluation.md`) is gated on Maher physically placing cubes. A synchronised RGB+depth capture harness `scripts/capture_rgb_depth_sync.py` exists (used for M4c1). `.gitignore` excludes `evaluation/camera_samples/` and `evaluation/bags/`; `evaluation/m4c_geometry_filter/` is intentionally NOT excluded (the report and the harness outputs are tracked).

M3 (ONNX export) and M4 (TensorRT FP16 engine on Jetson) both completed 2026-06-27. Artifacts: `models/best.onnx` (36.6 MB), `models/best.engine` (21.3 MB). M3 §3 export recipe and M4a trtexec recipe recorded in M3/M4 LOGBOOK entries.

M2 fallback training produced `models/best.pt`; see LOGBOOK 2026-06-24 M2 training entry and `models/README.md` for the artifact, training command, per-class mAP, and known caveats.

M1 hardware verification (camera topic + ML/runtime versions on the Jetson) is already complete and recorded in the 2026-06-23 M1 LOGBOOK entry. The M1 camera-topic verification did NOT check the depth topic; M4c1 added the live probe of `/depth_cam/depth/image_raw` (~30.5 Hz, 640×360 16UC1 mm) and confirmed `/depth_cam/depth_registered/points` does NOT exist on this install.

